<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Floating-overlay button styles (Spec 3 §3.2).

    Two narrow Material 3 button variants used exclusively by
    `overlay_5button_layout.xml`:

      - `OverlayButton.Primary` — the record/send button (text + leading
        icon). Filled `Widget.Material3.Button` ⇒ opaque `colorPrimary`
        container.
      - `OverlayButton.Icon` — Pause / Trash / Close (icon-only, 48 dp
        square). Filled-tonal icon button ⇒ opaque `colorSecondaryContainer`
        container.

    Both inherit Material 3 defaults — no `cornerRadius` override so the
    buttons match the keyboard-surface buttons (record_btn / trash_btn /
    pause_btn / enter_btn — none of them sets cornerRadius either, so
    they all share the Material 3 pill-shape default). The previous 12dp
    override was removed 2026-05-22 per user-req "Buttons sollen genauso
    ausschauen wie auf der normalen Tastatur, also auch mit den gleichen
    Rundungen".

    # Widget-transparency: buttons stay OPAQUE (2026-07-03)

    `Pref.WidgetOpacity` makes only the CARD fill translucent
    (`OverlayBackend.applyBackgroundOpacity` mutates the drawable fill).
    The buttons must NOT lose opacity — the translucent card may show
    through only BETWEEN the buttons.

    The original `OverlayButton.Icon` inherited
    `Widget.Material3.Button.IconButton`, a *standard* icon button whose
    container `backgroundTint` is `@android:color/transparent` (alpha 0).
    On an opaque card that reads fine (icon over surface), but once the
    card fill goes translucent the transparent-container buttons let the
    host content behind the card bleed straight through the whole button
    box — the user's "die Buttons verlieren auch die Deckkraft" report.
    The icons themselves stayed opaque; the button *background* was never
    opaque to begin with.

    Fix (systemic, one place): give the icon buttons a filled-tonal
    parent so their container is an opaque `colorSecondaryContainer`.
    Every overlay button now has an alpha-255 container tint, so the
    translucent card only shows in the gaps between the buttons — exactly
    the requested behaviour. Asserted in `OverlayBackendTest`
    ("overlay button backgrounds stay fully opaque at low widgetOpacity").

    @see docs/plans/2026-05-07 - dictate-keyboard-layout-refactor/research/3-floating-overlay/3-floating-overlay.reviewed.md §3.2
    @see docs/research/2026-07-02 - overlay-widget-transparency.md §3.3
-->
<resources>

    <style name="OverlayButton.Primary" parent="Widget.Material3.Button">
        <item name="android:textAllCaps">false</item>
    </style>

    <!-- Filled-tonal ⇒ opaque colorSecondaryContainer container. Keeps
         the M3 icon-button sizing/ripple/pill-shape while guaranteeing
         the button box stays fully opaque over a translucent card. -->
    <style name="OverlayButton.Icon" parent="Widget.Material3.Button.IconButton.Filled.Tonal" />

</resources>
